    "title": "Wisconsin Governer Tony Evers signed for flags to be flown at half-staff | News | fox21online.com",
    "text": "MADISON, Wis. (KQDS-TV) — Wisconsin Governer Tony Evers has ordered flags to be flown at half-staff.\nThe order will take effect on Monday, Aug. 10,2026 in honor of fallen Eau Claire firefighter Bryce A. Jungbluth.\nJungbluth died in the line of duty July 31, following a sudden medical incident.\nAccording to the governor’s office, Jungbluth was a dedicated public servant who was passionate about protecting others.\nHe is survived by his wife and their 9-month-old son.",
